  "notes": [
    "The standings image is the single richest name-to-chess.com-username source in the whole dataset.",
    "Qualification rules from the standings: A division top 14 make playoffs, top 10 get a one-round bye and the top 4 get two rounds; B division top 12 make playoffs with the top 4 getting a first-round bye.",
    "A division has an irregular draw as a result \u2014 it is not a clean power-of-two bracket. Rounds are numbered by the order they appear on the sheet.",
    "SCORES DELIBERATELY OMITTED. Both brackets print a single blue number per match rather than two scores, and the value varies (2, 2, 3 and 5 in the B division first round), so it is not a race to a fixed target. Unlike tournament 7, which shows both sides, there is no way to tell whether this number belongs to the winner or the loser. Recording it either way would be a guess, so all score fields here are null. The winners and the bracket structure are unaffected.",
    "A division bronze: the bracket prints 'Bronze medal game Nathan vs Matthew' with Matthew in bold, so Matthew took third.",
    "B division third place: '3rd place game Paul vs Jeff A' with Jeff A in bold.",
    "Division B row 18 is 'Free win', a placeholder rather than a person, and is dropped.",
    "Andy is listed as 'randiddly' here, confirming the correction noted in data/players.json.",
    "Round 2 slot 4 is Connor (6) vs Michael (11); Luis (3) meets Michael one round later. An earlier transcription duplicated the Luis match into round 2 and dropped Connor entirely."
  ],
